        "heading": "TOP SECRET SCIENCE (For Big and Small Brains)",
        "body": "Why do we have so many negative thoughts? Thousands of years ago, cavemen who thought \"That rustling bush is probably a deadly tiger!\" survived and ran away. Cavemen who thought \"It's probably just a cute bunny!\" got eaten. We inherited the brains of the nervous survivors! Your brain is an amazing danger-detector, but in the modern world, it often mistakes a school play for a hungry tiger."
      }
